  "arm": "dma batched",
  "note": "Does one cudaMemcpyBatchAsync of the group's uploads beat the loop of one-copy-each (STRATA_DMA_BATCH, F12)?  The first run of this sweep (bench/results/ab-dma-batch, 2026-10-22) did NOT answer it: the baseline left the variable unset and its counters read 0 on every window of all three launches - the submission path never ran there, so what got measured was copy-kernel against batch, not loop against batch.  Both arms still run --pcie-mode dma, for the same reason as before.  So BOTH arms now set the variable explicitly - 0 for the loop, 1 for the batch - and the run is void unless both sets of counters are non-zero.  The counters are exact (two atomics at the submission point, no noise floor applies): the loop is one submission per blob (~1 blob per submission), the batch one per group (far more).  One asymmetry is the code's own and cannot be arm-ed away: mode != 0 turns adaptive overlap off (generate.cpp:9501), so the arm is the flag as shipped - batch AND overlap off - against the loop WITH overlap.  That is the product question; the counters only say whether the batch itself ran.",
  "engine_arg": [
   "--pcie-mode",
   "dma"
  ],
  "engine_env": [
   "STRATA_DMA_BATCH=1"
  ],
  "command": "python tools/strata_bench.py --tests agent --config strata-instr.json --engine-arg \"--pcie-mode dma\" --engine-env STRATA_DMA_BATCH=1 --arm dma batched"
 },
